"""Per-repository template for tools/build_notebook.py (NOTEBOOK_SPEC 2.2 §4 standalone carrier).

Only the task-specific prose and stage cells live here. The isolated runtime, the embedded package (seven
modules, carried verbatim in dependency order), and the model pin/stage/verify cells are produced by
the generator from repository sources so they cannot drift from the package.

Generator /2.1 keys in use: ``modules`` lists every module of ``src/lightglue_pipeline/`` except
``__init__.py`` (``modeling.py`` is the vendored LightGlue + ALIKED network); ``entry_module`` is
``config.py`` (it holds ``MODEL_ID``/``MODEL_REVISION``/``MODEL_LICENSE`` and the model key under the
package's own spelling ``DEFAULT_MODEL_KEY``, mapped by ``identity_names``); ``model_host`` names the
two GitHub sources (the matcher from a release tag, the extractor from a pinned ALIKED commit) with its own
``pinned`` and ``access`` text (LGC-m2); ``rewrites`` carries two rules — the fleet ``DEFAULT_WEIGHTS_DIR``
rule and the ``__file__`` use inside ``model.resolve_weights_path``; ``model_load`` lets the pipeline pick
CUDA when it is visible. ``isolated_runtime`` (LGC-M1) installs the hash-locked pins into a uv environment
with a managed CPython 3.12.12 and routes every later cell there, so Run all needs no restart;
``infrastructure_labels`` and ``collapse_model_cell`` label and collapse Sections 1-3 (LGC-m6, GDL11).

This template configures an E2E image-matching fine-tuning workflow: the two pinned checkpoint pickles
are digest-verified, statically audited and converted once to safetensors, then loaded strictly into the
vendored network; 360 CC0 iNaturalist photographs are fetched with per-file digests and turned into
homography pairs with exact references (216 / 48 / 96 by photograph, two difficulty tiers — the hard tier
rotates up to ±150°, the regime the frozen matcher fails on); a drawn-shape pair is matched through the
inference contract; the frozen matcher is measured beside three baselines; a bounded fine-tuning of the
matcher's last layers and assignment head runs from the pinned base (Sections 5-7 reload the base first,
LGC-M2/M3); the held-out pairs are scored again per tier and the outcome is recorded, not asserted (LGC-m5);
the adapter is exported and reloaded; Section 10 is an off-by-default change-one-thing experiment on a fresh
copy of the base. Worked answers quote the recorded Kaggle Tesla T4 run of the previous notebook version
(LGC-m3), never the CPU build record as this run's result.
"""
