        "0.730 over epochs 0–3 and homography accuracy 0.729 → 0.688 → 0.708 → 0.667, differences of a few pairs in 48. So a "
        "gain here says the contract works; it does not say the adapted matcher is better on your images, that its confidences "
        "are calibrated, or that a match with a high confidence is right — it still returns matches for every pair, and it can "
        "be wrong confidently. Fine-tuning on a narrow set can also erode the model elsewhere; the drawn pair re-matched in "
        "Section 9 is one image of evidence about that, not a measurement.\n\n"
        "Three things to carry to real data. **Baselines first:** the identity guess, the patch neighbour, the descriptor "
        "neighbour and the frozen matcher's score on *your* pairs are the numbers to read before any adapted one, per tier and "
        "on the homography reading. **Leakage:** keep every photograph in one split (the contract de-duplicates by decoded "
        "pixels) and split by scene, session or photographer when your images come from few sources — the sample's observer "
        "overlap is printed for exactly that reason. **References:** a synthetic warp gives an exact `H`; real pairs need "
        "depth, pose or a fitted homography before they can be scored, and a fitted homography is itself an estimate.\n\n"
        "Successful execution proves that the recorded repository revision's package, carried in this standalone notebook, can "
        "acquire, digest-verify, audit and convert the pinned checkpoint pickles into its vendored network, fetch and "
        "digest-verify a real photograph set and build exact-reference pairs from it, validate the demonstrated dataset contract "
        "with a photograph-disjoint split, execute the inference contract and a bounded fine-tuning from the pinned base, "
        "evaluate against three baselines and the frozen model on an image-disjoint split, and emit the shown machine-readable "
        "artifacts — without the repository being reachable. It does **not** establish benchmark superiority, matching accuracy "
        "on real viewpoint changes, rotation invariance in general, other extractors or other cameras, calibration, or "
        "production fitness.\n\n"
        "**Optional experiments (they do not affect the default path):** Section 10 trains four layers on a fresh copy of the "
        "base. To try another setting through the main path instead, change one Section 7 field (`EPOCHS`, `LEARNING_RATE` "
        "— for example `1e-5` for a smaller, steadier change — or `TRAINABLE_LAYERS`), select Section 7 and choose **Run "
        "after**: Section 7 reloads the base before training, Section 8 compares against the same frozen score and adds a row "
        "to `run_history`, and Section 9 exports the new adapter. To try another split, change `SPLIT_SEED` in Section 4 and "
        "choose **Run after** there. To bring your own photographs, use BYOD (Section 4) and read the three baselines before "
        "the adapted number.\n\n"
        "## Troubleshooting\n\n"
        "- **Section 1 stops with \"needs a Linux x86_64 runtime\".** The locked environment is built from manylinux wheels. "
        "Use Google Colab, Kaggle or a Linux Jupyter server; Windows and macOS kernels are not supported.\n"
        "- **Section 1 fails while downloading** (`uv` wheel, Python build or packages). The runtime needs PyPI and the "
        "python-build-standalone download; run the cell again once the network is back. A \"size/SHA-256\" or \"does not "
        "match its digest\" error means a file was altered: do not edit the cell, regenerate the notebook from the "
        "repository.\n"
        "- **A stage seems stuck.** On CPU the baselines take about 20 minutes and the fine-tuning about 35 (more on a 2-vCPU "
        "runtime); watch for the `progress` lines, printed at least every 30 seconds. A GPU runtime (**Runtime → Change "
        "runtime type**) is faster, but the patch-neighbour baseline runs on the CPU on every runtime.\n"
        "- **\"The isolated environment's Python process exited\" or an out-of-memory error.** The runtime ran out of memory. "
        "Restart the session and choose **Run all**; in Section 7, `BATCH_SIZE = 2` needs less memory.\n"
        "- **A `sha256`/`size` `ValueError` or `FileNotFoundError` in Section 3.** A staged checkpoint is incomplete or altered "
        "— delete it from `weights/lightglue-aliked/` and run Section 3 again. A photograph digest mismatch in Section 4 is "
        "the same for the cache under `weights/inat-birds/`; a download error there means the iNaturalist bucket was "
        "unreachable — run Section 4 again.\n"
        "- **BYOD is refused in Section 4.** The message names what to fix: too few photographs for the split (at least 12 "
        "distinct photographs; it names the split that would be short), no JPEG / PNG files in the zip, a file that is not "
        "a zip or folder, or a path that does not exist. Fix it and run Section 4 with **Run after** again. An empty or "
        "cancelled upload, or a runtime without the Colab upload dialog, asks you to choose a file or set `BYOD_PATH`. Small "
        "photographs are not refused but reported as upscaled.\n"
        "- **Section 8 reads \"not above the frozen one\" or \"The selector kept epoch 0\".** Not an error: under these "
        "settings the adaptation did not beat the frozen matcher. Read the epoch history in Section 7; the export and reload "
        "in Section 9 still run.\n"
        "- **\"this pipeline already holds an adapted matcher\" from `adapt`.** Training starts from the pinned base only. "
        "Re-run Section 7 (it calls `reset_to_pretrained()` first) rather than calling `pipe.adapt` again by hand.\n"
        "- **Reload parity fails in Section 9.** The saved adapter does not reproduce the evaluated matcher. Re-run from "
        "Section 7, or restart the session and choose **Run all**.\n"
        "- **Numbers differ from the worked answers.** Frozen numbers move only in the third decimal between runtimes; the "
        "fine-tuning result by about a hundredth (Section 7, **Run-to-run spread**). Larger differences on the default "
        "settings mean a form field was changed.\n"
        "- **You re-ran the routing cell in Section 1.** It starts a new isolated process and discards every variable "
        "created so far; choose **Run all** again.\n\n"
        "## Glossary\n\n"
        "- **Keypoint / descriptor:** a distinctive image location (a corner, a blob) and the 128-number vector ALIKED computes "
        "to describe its neighbourhood.\n"
        "- **Sparse matching:** pairing keypoints of one image with keypoints of the other, rather than every pixel.\n"
        "- **Homography `H`:** the 3 × 3 matrix that maps image0 coordinates to image1 coordinates for a planar scene or a "
        "warped copy; here it is exact by construction.\n"
        "- **Reprojection error:** the distance in pixels between where a match puts a point in image1 and where `H` says it "
        "is.\n"
        "- **Precision at 3 px:** the share of returned matches with reprojection error under 3 px, averaged over pairs; an "
        "**inlier** is one such match.\n"
        "- **Homography accuracy:** the share of pairs whose homography fitted from the matches (RANSAC-DLT) moves the image "
        "corners by less than 3 (or 5) px against the reference.\n"
        "- **Confidence:** LightGlue's assignment score for a match — a ranking signal above a threshold, not a probability; "
        "the matcher never abstains.\n"
        "- **Identity / patch / descriptor baselines:** no-model and no-matcher references: same coordinates, best raw-pixel "
        "patch nearby, and ALIKED descriptors paired by mutual nearest neighbour.\n"
        "- **Easy / hard tier:** two families of synthetic warps; the hard tier rotates up to ±150°.\n"
        "- **Assignment loss:** the training objective — the negative log-likelihood of the correct match (or no-match) for "
        "every keypoint, from the reference `H`.\n"
        "- **Epoch / validation selection:** one pass over the training pairs; the epoch kept is the one with the highest "
        "validation precision at 3 px (epoch 0 = the frozen matcher).\n"
        "- **Training / validation / test split:** pairs used to train, to choose the epoch, and to report the final result "
        "once; split by photograph, so no photograph is in two splits.\n"
        "- **safetensors / adapter / reload parity:** a tensor file format that cannot run code when loaded; the saved trained "
        "tensors; and the check that a pipeline rebuilt from them and the pinned base gives the same matches.\n"
        "- **Pickle audit:** reading a checkpoint's pickle stream as data and refusing it unless it names only the four "
        "allowed constructors, before the weights-only unpickler opens it once.\n\n"
